  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trapca II Lund University - Trapca II Lund University 2</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Trapca II Lunds universitet</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lund University (LU) serves as the academic partner to Trapca (Trade  Policy Training Centre in Africa), a training center in Arusha,       Tanzania, with the aim of strengthening LDC trade policy capacity     through training, dialogue and networking. LU provides curricula and  course outlines, provides part of the education/training and is       responsible for examination and academic quality assuramce.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Lunds universitet (LU) fungerar som akademisk partner till Trapca    (Trade Policy Training Centre in Africa, ett utbildningscenter i      Arusha, Tanzania, med syfte att st&#xe4;rka MULs handelpolitiska kapacitet genom utbildning, dialog och n&#xe4;tverkande. LU st&#xe5;r f&#xf6;r kursuppl&#xe4;gg, en del av utbildningen samt examination.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lund University has been an academic partner to trapca. As the academic partner to ESAMI and trapca, LU is involved in the activities of trapca, contributes to and takes part in the various budget and reporting processes of trapca and has contributed also with inputs to the trapca completion report. LU appoints the Academic Director of trapca, who is part of the trapca management team and ex officio member of the trapca board. It is important to note that LU does not have an output of its own in the trapca project. lnstead, as a supporting institution LU has a share in the overall result of the centre.
The overall goal of trapca&apos;s offering is poverty reduction through improved integration in the world economy of LDCs and low-income sub-Saharan countries through enhancement of capacity (knowledge and skills) to negotiate and implement pro-poor trade policies and trade laws.
The programme objectives included:
Developing trade policy skills by conducting short courses in trade policy and international trade negotiations.Having an internationally anchored Centre with both African and internationally reputable trade institutional linkages.Organising top-level thematic and topical conferences on trade policy and law.Developing and delivering, a Master of Science Progamme in Trade Policy and Trade Law. Creating an efficient and effective network of a community of African and international trade experts to serve as faculty members. Building human and physical infrastructure capacity adequately to meet programme quality and service delivery standards and expectations.</narrative>
  </description>
